invariant: INV-17
file: gcm.c
catches: quic_test
builds: bin/quic_test
reason: gcm_open decrypts while it hashes, so a tag that does not match
  finds the plaintext already written. Without the wipe a failed open
  returns 0 and leaves that plaintext in the caller's buffer, and with it
  the keystream of the nonce, which is the plaintext exclusive-ored with
  ciphertext the sender chose. gcm.h promises zeros there
  (docs/decisions.md 85). The SP 800-38D vectors in test/gcm_tests.h
  forge one tag bit and require zeros after the call, so bin/quic_test
  is what objects.

--- old
    if (!ok) {
        ct_wipe(pt, n);
        return 0;
    }
--- new
    if (!ok) {
        return 0;
    }
